# device_create_nothing_dies_on_root_page: No task callbacks and no memory map: the device is created, its registers work, and the first nonzero root-page write finds no create_task callback: the host dies. Map setup only: the runner installs no task callbacks there, and without a map it has nothing else.
{"descriptor": {"no_map": true}, "op": "config", "ram": [["0x40000000", "0x4000000"]], "stamp_slots": 2, "watchdog_s": 30}
{"off": "0x1034", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0xf5"}
{"from": "0x1000", "label": "no blocks, no map", "op": "mmio_sweep", "step": 4, "to": "0x1300"}
{"off": "0x101c", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x0"}
{"label": "root page 0 is harmless", "off": "0x101c", "op": "mmio_r"}
{"off": "0x101c", "op": "mmio_w", "val": "0x10001"}
